@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Support Law, 5741-1980 (חוק הבטחת הכנסה): the gate to a benefit. Row IL-33.
-- Source: ../../../income-support-law-5741-1980/registers/source-bundle/income-support-law-5741-1980.he.wiki.txt
-- (Hebrew Wikisource raw wikitext). Every `src:N` comment in this module quotes line N of THAT file.
--
-- WHAT IT IS FOR. s 68(c) of the National Insurance Law adds a supplement to the child allowance of a parent
-- "paid for a given month a benefit under the Income Support Law". Row IL-06 takes that fact as an input.
-- This module says when a benefit is paid for a month, as far as the Law's gate goes:
--   s 2(a)  who is entitled: a resident of 25 or over on one of the grounds (1) to (9), or on a ground of the
--           First Schedule at any age (2A); s 2(b) resident for 24 consecutive months before the claim, unless
--           a pension is paid under Chapter 5 or 11 of the Insurance Law;
--   s 3     who is not entitled;
--   s 4(a)  a person's entitlement needs the s 2 conditions of his spouse too;
--   s 5(b), s 7(b), s 8  the amount: the benefit for a person without income less the income, held to the
--           difference between the income and the determining sum, and not paid if under 6 shekels unless a
--           pension is paid;
--   s 14(a) payment starts on the 1st of the month of the claim;
--   s 14A(a) none for a month spent wholly abroad.
-- "Resident" is the Insurance Law's s 2A (s 23(a) of this Law applies it with the changes required).
--
-- NOT ENCODED (NOTES.md has the reasons): the grounds (1) to (3) and (7) as the Law's regulations fix them; the
-- Second Schedule's rates (so the benefit for a person without income is an input); Chapter 4's income (ss 9 to
-- 12) and the deductions; s 6 (couples' amounts); the determining sums of s 7(a) (regulations); ss 14A(b) to (g);
-- ss 14B, 15 to 32.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Income Support Law — whether a benefit is paid for a month`

§§ `Section 2: who is entitled`

-- src:78 | (א) תושב ישראל שמלאו לו 25 שנים זכאי לגימלה, בכפוף להוראות חוק זה, כל עוד מתקיים בו אחד מתנאים אלה:
-- src:96 | (ב) תנאי נוסף לזכאות לגימלה הוא שהתובע היה תושב ישראל עשרים וארבעה חדשים רצופים לפני הגשת תביעתו, אולם תנאי זה לא יחול על מי שמקבל קיצבה לפי פרק ה׳ או פרק י״א לחוק הביטוח.
-- The 25 years: "מלאו לו 25 שנים": completed, 300 months.
@ref ISL s 2(a), (b), (2A), lines 78-96
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      f         IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` p `with` f `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        (   (f's `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`)
         OR `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`))
    AND (   (f's `a ground of the First Schedule under section 2(a)(2A) holds`)
         OR (    `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` 300 `on` `the day` `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)
             AND (   count (f's `grounds under section 2(a)(1), (2), (3), (5), (7), (8) and (9) that hold`) GREATER THAN 0
                  OR `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd)))
    AND (   (f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`)
         OR (f's `was a resident of Israel for the 24 consecutive months before the claim`))

§§ `Section 3: who is not entitled`

-- src:105 | לא יהיו זכאים לגימלה לפי חוק זה –
-- src:106 | (1) אדם הנמצא במוסד וכל החזקתו היא על חשבון אוצר המדינה, הסוכנות היהודית לארץ ישראל, רשות מקומית או גוף אחר שנקבע בתקנות;
-- src:107 | (2) אדם המשרת שירות סדיר בצבא־הגנה לישראל ואשתו;
-- src:108 | (3) חבר בתאגיד האחראי לכלכלת חבריו;
-- src:109 | (4) תלמיד הלומד במוסד שקבע השר בתקנות ובתנאים שקבע, למעט –
-- src:110 | (א) מי שמשתלמת לו גמלה לפי פסקה (4) של סעיף 2(א);
-- src:121 | (א) מי שנדון למאסר בשל עבירת רצח או ניסיון לרצח בנסיבות טרור לא יהיה זכאי לגמלה המשולמת לפי חוק זה, הוא לא יובא בחשבון כבן זוג לעניין גמלה לפי חוק זה, למעט לעניין סעיף 11, ובן זוגו לא ייחשב הורה עצמאי לעניין חוק זה.
@ref ISL s 3(1) to (4), s 3C, lines 106-109, 121
GIVEN f IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ISL s 3 — barred by section 3 or 3C:` f MEANS
        f's `is in an institution maintained wholly at the expense of the State or another named body, section 3(1)`
    OR  f's `serves regular service in the Israel Defense Forces, or is the wife of one who does, section 3(2)`
    OR  f's `is a member of a corporation responsible for the livelihood of its members, section 3(3)`
    OR  f's `is a student at an institution the Minister fixed, and not within the exceptions of section 3(4)(a) and (b)`
    OR  f's `is barred by section 3C (a conviction for a terror offence)`

§§ `Section 4(a): a couple`

-- src:126 | (א) הזכאות לגימלה של כל אחד מבני זוג מותנית בכך שמתקיימים גם בבן זוגו תנאי הזכאות לפי סעיף 2.
-- "הזכאות לגימלה של כל אחד מבני זוג מותנית בכך שמתקיימים גם בבן זוגו תנאי הזכאות לפי סעיף 2." The spouse's
-- conditions are those of s 2, not of s 3. Section 4(b) (persons the Minister excluded by regulation) is not
-- deposited.
@ref ISL s 4(a), line 126
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      f         IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
      spouse    IS A MAYBE `A claimant under the Income Support Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` p `with` f `and a spouse` spouse `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` p `with` f `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    AND NOT `ISL s 3 — barred by section 3 or 3C:` f
    AND CONSIDER spouse
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST pr THEN `ISL s 2 — the s 2 conditions are met by` (pr's `the person`) `with` (pr's `the facts`) `, on` `the day` `, reading` rd

§§ `Sections 5(b), 7(b), 8, 14(a), 14A(a): what is paid for a month`

-- src:138 | (ב) הגימלה לזכאי שיש לו הכנסה תהיה בסכום השווה להפרש שבין הגימלה, שהיה זכאי לה לפי סעיפים קטנים (א) או (ה) לולא ההכנסה, לבין ההכנסה.
-- src:163 | (ב) זכאי שהכנסתו, המחושבת לפי סעיפים 9 עד 11, אינה נמוכה מהסכום הקובע החל לגביו – לא תשולם לו גימלה; זכאי שהכנסתו כאמור נמוכה מהסכום הקובע החל לגביו, תשולם לו גימלה לפי סעיפים 5 או 6, לפי הענין, אשר סכומה לא יעלה על ההפרש שבין הכנסתו לבין הסכום הקובע.
-- src:167 | גימלה שהיא פחותה מששה שקלים חדשים לא תשולם אלא אם הזכאי לה מקבל קיצבה לפי חוק הביטוח.
-- src:267 | (א) גימלה תשולם רק בעד התקופה שתחילתה ב־1 לחודש שבו הוגשה למוסד לביטוח לאומי התביעה לגימלה, ואולם השר רשאי לקבוע בתקנות נסיבות שבהן תשולם הגימלה ממועד מוקדם יותר ולתקופה שקבע.
-- src:273 | (א) לא תשולם לזכאי שיצא את ישראל גמלה בעד חודש קלנדרי אם שהה מחוץ לישראל בכל הימים שבאותו חודש. לענין סעיף קטן זה וסעיפים קטנים (ב) ו־(ג), ”זכאי“ – למעט זכאי שהוא או בן זוגו הגיעו לגיל פרישה.
-- s 5(b): to one with income the benefit is the difference between the benefit he would have had without
-- income and the income. s 7(b): one whose income is not below the determining sum is paid nothing; one whose
-- income is below it is paid a benefit not above the difference between his income and the determining sum.
-- s 7(c) takes out of s 7: one paid a benefit under s 5(a)(2)(a) (under 55 and paid no pension), one who
-- reached the retirement age, and couples. s 8: under 6 new shekels is not paid unless the claimant receives
-- a pension under the Insurance Law. s 14(a): payment is only for the period starting on the 1st of the month
-- of the claim. s 14A(a): none for a month spent wholly outside Israel (for one who is not of or married to
-- retirement age; the exception is not encoded).
@ref ISL s 5(b), 7(b), 7(c), 8, 14(a), 14A(a), lines 138, 163-164, 167, 267, 273
GIVEN `the first day of the month` IS A DATE
      p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      f         IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
      m         IS A `The money of a month under the Income Support Law`
      couple    IS A BOOLEAN
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` `the first day of the month` `, of` p `with` f `and` m `, a couple:` couple `, reading` rd MEANS
    IF   `the first day of the month` LESS THAN (m's `the first day of the month in which the claim was submitted`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   f's `stayed outside Israel on every day of the month, section 14A(a)`
         THEN 0
         ELSE IF   benefit LESS THAN 6 AND NOT (f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`)
              THEN 0
              ELSE benefit
    WHERE
        withoutIncome MEANS m's `the benefit for a person without income, from the Second Schedule`
        income        MEANS m's `the income, computed under sections 9 to 12`
        afterIncome   MEANS max 0 (withoutIncome MINUS income)
        section7Applies MEANS
                NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the first day of the month` `, reading` rd
            AND NOT couple
            AND (   `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` 660 `on` `the first day of the month` `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)
                 OR f's `receives a pension under Chapter 5 or Chapter 11 of the Insurance Law`)
        benefit MEANS
            IF   section7Applies
            THEN CONSIDER (m's `the determining sum that applies to the claimant under section 7(a), if regulations fix one`)
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN afterIncome
                 WHEN JUST ds THEN
                     IF   income AT LEAST ds
                     THEN 0
                     ELSE min afterIncome (ds MINUS income)
            ELSE afterIncome

@ref ISL s 5(b), 7(b), 8, 14(a), 14A(a); the ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the first day of the month` IS A DATE
      p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      f         IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
      m         IS A `The money of a month under the Income Support Law`
      couple    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` `the first day of the month` `, of` p `with` f `and` m `, a couple:` couple MEANS
    `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` `the first day of the month` `, of` p `with` f `and` m `, a couple:` couple `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

-- A benefit under the Income Support Law is paid for the month if the claimant is entitled (ss 2 to 4) and the
-- amount computed is above nothing.
@ref ISL s 2 to 8, 14, 14A
GIVEN `the first day of the month` IS A DATE
      p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      f         IS A `The facts of a claimant under the Income Support Law`
      spouse    IS A MAYBE `A claimant under the Income Support Law`
      m         IS A `The money of a month under the Income Support Law`
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ISL — a benefit is paid for the month beginning` `the first day of the month` `to` p `with` f `, a spouse` spouse `and` m `, reading` rd MEANS
        `ISL s 2 to 4 — entitled to a benefit:` p `with` f `and a spouse` spouse `, on` `the first day of the month` `, reading` rd
    AND computed GREATER THAN 0
    WHERE
        isCouple MEANS
            CONSIDER spouse
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE
        computed MEANS `ISL — the benefit computed for the month beginning` `the first day of the month` `, of` p `with` f `and` m `, a couple:` isCouple `, reading` rd
